The expanded `solutionProgram` macro is byte-identical at the KAST level to the freshly translated `solution.mpy`, so the entry claim does pin the submitted AST. The main soundness issue is instead in execution: the proof adds priority bridges around symbolic splitting, iteration, and `len`; I’m now testing those bridges and the fresh false-result mutation independently.
